  "title": "Alexa's Conjecture on Primality",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Definition Let $r_i$ be the unique integer (with respect to a fixed $p\\in\\mathbb{N}$ ) such that\n\n$$(2i+1)^{p-1} \\equiv r_i \\pmod p ~~\\text{ and } ~ 0 \\le r_i < p.$$\n\nConjecture A natural number $p \\ge 8$ is a prime iff $$\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{\\left \\lfloor \\frac{\\sqrt[3]p}{2} \\right \\rfloor} r_i = \\left \\lfloor \\frac{\\sqrt[3]p}{2} \\right \\rfloor$$",
